          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: inconclusive—cost-event records unavailable\n\nI confirmed the relevant Racine work order and the exact September Pending Close timestamp. However, the authorized records contain **no cost-event rows**, and the supporting records were **not staged and restricted to the records-custodian role**. Consequently, I cannot establish whether a late-created event exists or verify its transaction details.\n\n| Required finding | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine, Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Unavailable |\n| Event amount | Unavailable—not assumed to be zero |\n| Exact event-created time | Unavailable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot be calculated without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Unavailable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe source timestamp does not specify a timezone or UTC offset; I have not assumed one. These confirmed facts come from the supplied `work_orders` and `cost_periods` records.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied **Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B** excerpt, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” printed page **225** / PDF page **233**, states:\n\n> “Transactions created after the pending close date, even if they relate to a current or prior period, won't be processed.”\n\nSuch new transactions are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting until the period is closed or reopened. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue to be processed.\n\nThus, a non-exempt September transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should remain unprocessed while the period is Pending Close. Without the event’s type and recorded accounting status, a transaction-specific consistency conclusion would be unsupported.\n\n**Missing event rows do not demonstrate that no late event occurred.** I submitted the report as incomplete (`needs_evidence`) and saved the findings and provenance at:\n\n`/cache/work/worker_b53799613deb/audit-report.json`\n\n**No database records were changed.**",
